      "op": "note",
      "text": "person_d1 (2026-11-11, person-play-d1): day 1 played as the tutorial tells a new player, by real input only. The tutorial stays ON. No cheat, no DecideCorrectly, no game call in place of a click on the desk. RIG HELP: one game call, RunManager.LoadTitleScene (the call step before the 1280x1024 run), returns to the Title between the two runs, because the office has no Quit to Title control (a game finding). The stamp of each case comes from the compare readouts on the screen (personReadout, personDecide, stampAim text readout), never from the case's truth or the colour of a line: the TEXT of the readout decides for every compare, and an empty readout fails the step. Cases 1 to 3 at 1920x1080, then a new run at 1280x1024 and case 1 again. Each case ends by a real stamp drag and a real hand-back drag and personVerdict asserts it was scored correct with no citation slip. The game findings are in person_report.txt (FINDING lines). Inspect mode (SPACE) is left again before the stamp. Rig help, where a step cannot be done by real input, is said in the report as RIG HELP. The 1280x1024 stamp lands on the point under the pointer at the let-go (3 mm limit): the reading view eases its camera while the dater is carried, and stampAim judges the landing against the pointer's point at the let-go."
